I'm currently playing my first succesful wizard (just arrived at the 
VS), and he wasn't special (in fact, he got lousy starting equipment). 
What I do:

* Use your pet, especially for the very low level monsters (level your 
pet, but they don't help you) and the very tough ones. Heal him if you can.
* Engrave Elbereth if you're in a really tough spot, like the inevitable 
ants you mention.
* Use daggers. Advance your dagger skill as far as possible, and find a 
nice stack of daggers to throw. Especially if they are enchanted up (or 
you find a few that are enchanted) they are a formidable weapon at the 
higher skills.
* I usually go to Sokoban first (maybe one level of the mines for some 
armor and daggers) to alleviate the food problem, and get my strength up.
* Try to get some means of escape, like ?oTele or /oDig. Don't be 
affraid to retreat and wait for HP and/or SP to get back up.
* Use all your spells, not just force bolt/magic missile. Sleep can be a 
very powerful spell, protection can save you, remove curse allows you to 
try out all armor without b/u/c id'ing it, etc.
* This is probably not useful early on, but you can get spellbooks in 
many ways: saccing and praying, polying, killing priests, getting 
crowned, writing them (you have a very high chance of success for 
writing unknown spellbooks).

That should get you to the quest, after which, especially if you have 
Magicbane, you're pretty much invulnerable, I've noticed.

